    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T22:49:12Z",
    "body": "Pushed c3be0a2c on issue/1256-escape-closes (test-only, one file: `escape_tests.rs`). Item by item:\n\n1. **Fixture dialog, `escape_closes_the_fixture_dialog_without_applying`:** a pending edit (`SaveFixtureDraft.note`) is now set in the open draft and checked before Escape. After Escape the dialog is gone, and no library file exists. Escape closes the draft with its dialog, so there is no open draft left for the value to live in. The test pins that the edit is never written and the dialog closes.\n2. **Fixture dialog below the prompt, `escape_closes_only_the_topmost_dialog_per_press`:** same pending note, checked to be unchanged after the first press (the prompt closes, the draft stays open with the edit), then the second press closes the dialog and writes no library file.\n3. **Unsaved prompt, document not replaced:** the test sets `project_path` to a named document before the press and asserts it is still that document after the press. `NewDocument` clears `project_path`, so this would fail if Cancel ever ran the New path.\n\nNot covered (as before, not blocking): the Insert, Vise, Plate and Accessory variants of `FixtureLibDialog`, the egui `Window` panels, and the pick-draft and box-select Escape items named in the issue's \"Done means\". The decision note should say the pick-draft item is outside this PR.\n\nGate: `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib escape` 3/3 pass; `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (ui suites, 15s); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nReady for a re-review.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
